most important part of your business, treat them well and they will treat the customer well. Don't be afraid to be short handed by getting rid of bad managers or employees.","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"restaurant staff turnover","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/small-restaurant-habits-increase-revenue-profits-bimpos-aygqe/","authorName":"John Balian✔","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"★POS Expert ★Franchise Management ★Business Development ★Visionary Entrepreneur ★Product Manager ★Learner","company":"BIM POS","location":"Not specified","postText":"Small daily habits can make a big difference in restaurant profitability. Better upselling, staff training, table turnover, and inventory control all contribute to stronger results. The right tools turn these habits into measurable, sustainable growth.","reactionCount":4,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"restaurant staff turnover","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/we-track-food-waste-penny-so-why-ignoring-cost-empty-chair-blum-cpc-9ubye/","authorName":"Brian Blum CPC","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Executive Restaurant & Chef Search | Gecko Hospitality | Connecting New England's Top Culinary Talent | Building World-Class Restaurant Teams in New England |Die-Hard Patriots Fan","company":"Gecko Hospitality","location":"New England","postText":"We track food waste to the penny. So why do we ignore the cost of an empty GM chair? In hospitality, an open leadership role isn't just an inconvenience. It's a daily drain on your bottom line. Every shift without the right person in charge puts pressure on your supervisors, your guest experience, and your bottom line. The ripple effects are real: Overworked shift supervisors Declining guest experience standards Increased hourly staff turnover Missed catering and event revenue Sourcing elite leadership talent isn't just an HR function. It is a core operational strategy. The right General Manager or Executive Chef doesn't appear on a job board. They have to be found, approached, and carefully assessed for fit. Read the full article below and share your thoughts in the comments. I'd love to hear how your organization approaches leadership hiring. #HospitalityLeadership #RestaurantManagement #TalentSourcing #ExecutiveRecruiting","reactionCount":5,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"restaurant staff turnover","postUrl":"","authorName":"Giavanna U.","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"M.S. BCBA. LBA., CEO at True Care Behavior, Founder of getRBTcertified","company":"True Care Behavior","location":"Not specified","postText":"In 2024, enterprise organizations averaged 103% employee turnover. Mid-size was 89% while small was 77%. (CentralReach 2025 Autism and IDD Care Market Report) Hospital staff turnover that year ran about 21%. Some companies in our field are replacing their entire workforce annually and calling it a staffing challenge. Here is what it looks like clinically: an RBT quits and a child loses their therapist. That kid starts over with a stranger, rebuilds trust from zero, and gives back weeks of progress that took months to earn. Turnover shows up in a spreadsheet as a labor cost. Ask RBTs why they left and you rarely hear “the kids.” You hear cancelled sessions, schedules that change every week, onboarding that lasted three days, and a BCBA who was too buried under 40 cases to ever show up. That last one is the one a company actually control.","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"restaurant staff turnover","postUrl":"","authorName":"Noblexus","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Not applicable (Company page)","company":"Noblexus","location":"Not specified","postText":"Restaurants and cafes have some of the highest staff turnover of any industry — which means, over a few years, a number of former employees may still technically have access to your POS system, your reservations platform, or your guest Wi-Fi admin panel, long after their last shift. That's not anyone being careless. It's just what happens when onboarding a new hire during a rush is urgent, and offboarding someone who's already gone quietly slips down the list. A readiness assessment starts with something simple: mapping what systems you actually have, and who can still get into them. Most owners are surprised by the gap between what they assumed and what's actually true. None of this requires a security background to fix. It requires someone actually checking — which is different from assuming everything's fine because nothing's gone wrong yet. If you added up every former employee who might still have a working login somewhere, what would that number be? #Hospitality #Restaurants #DigitalReadiness #AccessControl #BCBusiness","reactionCount":7,"commentCount":2,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"restaurant staff turnover","postUrl":"","authorName":"Jane Parmel","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Business Wealth Architect™ Redesigning Established Companies for Greater Profit, Stronger Leadership, Owner Freedom & Transferable Value | Restaurant, Hospitality & Service-Based Businesses","company":"Not specified","location":"Not specified","postText":"New data from HeyHire confirms 78% of restaurants entered 2026 understaffed, with an average time-to-fill of 21 days per open role and annual turnover hovering at 75%. The National Restaurant Association notes full-service employment remains 183,000 jobs below pre-pandemic February 2020 levels. Restaurants without documented SOPs, training workflows, and retention strategies are caught in a costly and demoralizing cycle. Want to know how we can change that in your restaurant? hotel? bar? food service company? #BusinessWealthArchitect #ProfitGrowth #Restaurant #Hospitality #BusinessDevelopment #ProfitGPS #Advisory #Staffing #Team","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-02","interactions":[]}]}


