{"posts":[{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bhavanicodes/","authorName":"Bhavani Ravi","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bhavanicodes/","jobTitle":"I use open-source to attack the data chaos | Apache Airflow Champion | International Tech Speaker","company":"N/A","location":"Not shown","postText":"I'm super scared to see how small businesses are handling PII (Personally Identifiable Information) in the AI world. You should not dump your customers' info as-is into an AI system without their consent. You should strip it off outside the system. Even with an enterprise subscription, you cannot control what leaves your system. Data masking looks something like this \"John Doe (ID: 4819) called about a billing issue on his visa ending in 1234.\" to \"Patient_1 (ID: ID_Var1) called about a billing issue on his Card_Type_1 ending in Digits_1.\" There are a few privacy guard tools for Claude. If you have any trusted tools that you use for your AI agents, drop them in your comments … more","reactionCount":20,"commentCount":9,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[{"interaction_type":"comment","user_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/akshay-jingar/","username":"Akshay jingar","value":"Indeed during my visit to one of the chemical factory. I observe that the engineer use extensive AI to build a generate insights and dashboard and he just share all the customer details plus sales to feed AI prompt. I guess this is the High time to make aware of PII in Indian.","time":"19h","comment_reply_to_user_url":null},{"interaction_type":"comment","user_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/bhavanicodes/","username":"Bhavani Ravi","value":"Sad and scary","time":"16h","comment_reply_to_user_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/akshay-jingar/"},{"interaction_type":"comment","user_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sowmyalr/","username":"Sowmya L R","value":"One pattern I'd add to this thread: if you're building for scale, PII redaction is best handled upstream in the data pipeline, not bolted on as a prompt-level guardrail. Data Prep Kit's pii_redactor transform is a solid open-source reference — Presidio for detection, Flair for entity recognition, configurable entity types and redact/replace modes, and it scales from a laptop to a full ingestion pipeline.","time":"14h","comment_reply_to_user_url":null}]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/decision-latency-sell-side-firms-rarely-measure-datazoic-alzbc/","authorName":"Datazoic Inc.","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/datazoic/posts/","jobTitle":"N/A","company":"Datazoic Inc.","location":"Not shown","postText":"Most conversations about data fragmentation in capital markets focus on volume. How many systems, how many touchpoints, how much reconciliation. Less discussed is when the picture actually arrives. A client engages with research. The same client shifts their flow. Both recorded, both accurate — and they reach the salesperson who owns the relationship days apart. Neither data collection nor recording has failed. But the moment to take action still passed. That gap has a name, and a cost. New piece on decision latency in sell-side client coverage. How are you handling it on your desk — more discipline in the pre-call process, or something structural?","reactionCount":6,"commentCount":2,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7500229278370938881/","authorName":"Robert Broeckelmann, CISSP","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/robert-broeckelmann-cissp-7567b517/","jobTitle":"Identity Architecture | IAM | Application Security | AI Security Consultant | Managing Director","company":"IYA CyberSecurity Solutions","location":"Not shown","postText":"Aura sells identity theft protection for a living. In March 2026, one employee took a single convincing phone call, and 900,000 of Aura's own customer records ended up on a dark web leak site a few hours later. The attacker didn't breach a firewall or crack an encryption scheme. They called an employee, impersonated someone with legitimate reason to ask for access, and got it. ShinyHunters claimed the breach; Have I Been Pwned later confirmed the scope: names, home addresses, phone numbers, emails, pulled from Aura's marketing database. Here's what most incident retrospectives skip: the access itself only lasted about an hour before Aura's team shut it down. That's actually the more useful number than 'was MFA enabled.' The question that matters is how fast you can kill a live session once you know it's live, not whether you had a policy that said you should be able to. Microsoft and several major IdPs now support Continuous Access Evaluation, which re-checks session validity in near real time instead of waiting for a token to expire on its own schedule. Most organizations have it available and never turned it on. Mean time to revoke is the metric worth tracking. Most companies have never measured it. That gap is the actual audit finding, not whether MFA was technically turned on.","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:ugcPost:7500692470465384449/","authorName":"Sparq","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/teamsparq/posts/","jobTitle":"N/A","company":"Sparq","location":"Not shown","postText":"Fragmented Data is thrilled to report that Q3 went both better and worse than expected!","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"","authorName":"Joe Dallacqua","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/joe-dallacqua-8390b36/","jobTitle":"Senior Principal Solutions Consultant","company":"Sparq","location":"Not shown","postText":"From Legacy Stack to Fragmented Data - it's time to start to address the problems directly. Let's get 'em on the couch and figure out what's going on there. Welcome episode 2 of Sparq's We're Into That series. #EnterpriseAI #ConnectedData #DigitalEngineering #WereIntoThat","reactionCount":5,"commentCount":3,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/reducing-your-business-exposure-cyber-risk-databench-australia-icmpc/","authorName":"DataBench","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/databench-australia/posts/","jobTitle":"N/A","company":"DataBench","location":"Not shown","postText":"Reducing your business exposure to cyber risks starts by understanding the relationship between personal data and cyber risks. To understand more, take a look at this week's blog here: Reducing Your Business Exposure to Cyber Risk","reactionCount":3,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"","authorName":"Ammaar Salih","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ammaarsalih/","jobTitle":"Cyber Security Strategist | Leading Enterprise Threat Hunting & Defense","company":"N/A","location":"Not shown","postText":"A phishing service called NovaCookies sells stolen Microsoft 365 sessions for $320 a month. It is adversary in the middle tooling packaged as a subscription. The attacker relays the victim through a proxy, captures the authenticated session token after login succeeds, and walks straight past multifactor authentication because the challenge was already answered by the real user. Password plus MFA was never the finish line, and pricing like this makes that plain. When session theft costs less than a mid tier software licence, the barrier to entry has effectively gone. My view is that the defensive centre of gravity moves to token binding, conditional access tied to device compliance, shorter session lifetimes, and detections built on anomalous session reuse rather than impossible travel. If a valid session token belonging to one of your executives were replayed from an unmanaged device tonight, which control would actually catch it?","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"","authorName":"Aditya Kusuma","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/adityakusuma/","jobTitle":"Performance Marketing | Meta & Google Ads | AI Marketing Strategist","company":"N/A","location":"Not shown","postText":"He walked back into chest-deep water. It was 17:00, shift change. The rain had been heavy for two hours, but nobody expected the factory yard to disappear. I was there to review the ad account. My client told all 120 employees to evacuate to the upper floor. Then he went back alone. He came out carrying the old server. The one with three years of conversion data, the pixel history, every order record that proves which ad actually paid for payroll. Water was dripping from his chin. He set it on a dry table and said: 'Backup everything tonight.' No speech. No hero pose. Just a man who understood his numbers were never abstract to begin with. They are payroll for 120 families. They are the 11 PM calls. They are the reason he sleeps four hours a night. The dashboard shows the ROAS. It will never show what it took to keep that data alive. When did you last see the person behind the numbers you rely on?","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"","authorName":"Shaffan Khan","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaffan-khan/","jobTitle":"Financial Analyst | Financial Statement Analysis | Valuation | FP&A | Financial Modeling","company":"N/A","location":"Not shown","postText":"Everyone is busy worrying about AI. But what if the bigger risk is happening quietly across borders? AI is definitely changing India's IT sector but I think there's another risk worth watching that is Geopolitical fragmentation. India's IT success was built on a simple model: global clients, Indian talent and seamless cross-border delivery. But trade tensions, data localisation, stricter regulations, local hiring and rising GCC capabilities could slowly change that equation. The real question isn't whether technology work will disappear, it's whether more of that work will need to happen closer to the client. And if that happens, India's traditional delivery advantage could look very different.","reactionCount":61,"commentCount":37,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"Client data fragmentation","postUrl":"","authorName":"Eric P. Laughery","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/ericlaughery/","jobTitle":"IT Executive (Director/VP/CIO) | 25+ M&A Integrations, Zero Disruption","company":"N/A","location":"Not shown","postText":"Call Impersonation fraud Do not panic, hang up the phone, and call them back using the phone number on the back of your card. If it's real, you now KNOW who you are talking to. Do not trust anyone who calls you. If they try to scare you into a decision, do not respond; hang up.","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]}]}


