{"posts":[{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Kunal Zagde","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kunalzagde/","jobTitle":"Offshore support for UK Advisers | Founder","company":"","location":"","postText":"UK IFAs — nobody started their firm to chase the same missing document three times. But talk to enough early-stage advisers and that's basically the job description by Wednesday. Client file admin. Chasing documents. Data entry into the back-office system. Diary and inbox management. The stuff that has to happen before a suitability report can even get started. That's usually where the hours actually go — not the technical work most people assume is the bottleneck. It's also the easiest place to build offshore capacity properly — trained to your process, managed end-to-end, without the £40k+ commitment of a full-time UK hire. If your week looks like this, I'd be glad to talk through what a setup like this could look like for your firm. #FinancialAdvisers #Paraplanning #IFA #OffshoreStaffing #FinancialServices","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Shweta Dedhia","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/shweta-dedhia/","jobTitle":"Executive Search & Talent Acquisition Professional Specializing in Banking, Financial Services & Insurance Hiring","company":"","location":"","postText":"Hiring: Cluster Manager – Independent Financial Advisor (IFA)| Retail Sales. Company: Leading Asset Management Co. Location: Mumbai. Department: Retail Sales. Reporting to: Channel Head. We are looking for an experienced Cluster Manager – IFA to drive sales and distribution through a set of assigned distributors and build strong, long-term relationships within the mutual fund/financial services ecosystem. Key Responsibilities: Manage sales & distribution for assigned distributors, Drive revenue generation and achieve sales targets, Build and maintain strong relationships with key distributors, Advise distributors on suitable products based on customer/investor requirements, Ensure effective distributor servicing and timely query resolution, Stay updated on mutual fund products, capital markets and market trends, Maintain distributor data and identify opportunities for repetitive business, Collaborate with senior sales representatives to close business opportunities, Manage and develop the team. Ideal Candidate: MBA – Finance / Marketing, 10+ years of experience in the financial services industry, preferably Mutual Funds, Strong understanding of capital markets, Excellent distributor/client management skills, Result-oriented with strong entrepreneurial and interpersonal skills, Target-oriented with strong compliance orientation. Interested candidates can share their CV at shweta@rightmatch.co.in","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Mtwa Mpogole","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mtwa-mpogole-5a9b59348/","jobTitle":"Founder & Managing Director | MILLENIBANK | Designing the Next Generation of African Digital Finance | Fintech • AI • Payments • Cybersecurity | Investors • Partners • Co-Founders","company":"","location":"","postText":"Can Data Become a Financial Asset Without Becoming a Threat to Customers? As financial services become increasingly digital, data will play an enormous role in how institutions understand customers, manage risk, detect fraud, and improve services. But this creates an important question: How do we use financial data to create value while protecting the people who generate it? This is an issue I consider fundamental to the long-term vision of MILLENIBANK Tanzania Limited. Responsible data use could help financial institutions better understand customer needs, improve financial products, identify unusual activity, and provide more relevant financial insights. For SMEs, data could potentially help create a clearer picture of business activity and financial performance. But data should never be treated as something an institution can exploit simply because it has access to it. It must be governed carefully. That means thinking seriously about: Privacy and consent, Data security, Access controls, Purpose limitation, Transparency, Responsible AI, Fraud prevention, Regulatory compliance, Data quality and accuracy. There is also an important philosophical principle: The customer should not lose control simply because their financial life has become digital. Technology should give people greater capability—not make them less informed about how their information is being used. For MILLENIBANK, the ambition is therefore not to collect as much data as possible. It is to explore how the right data, used responsibly, can create genuine value for customers and businesses.","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Hemal Kardani","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/hemal-kardani-aveva-pi/","jobTitle":"AVEVA PI System Architecture & Administration | Custom PI Development — AF SDK, PI Web API, PI Vision | OT/IT Data Integration | Industrial AI/ML","company":"","location":"","postText":"One thing I've learned while working with industrial data: Having data is not the same as having useful data. With AVEVA PI System and industrial historian environments, I've seen how small things can create bigger problems later — incorrect tags, poor data quality, unorganized assets, slow queries, or simply not knowing when something has gone wrong. My usual way of looking at it is pretty simple: Collect → Validate → Organize → Monitor → Analyze. If the foundation is right, everything built on top of it becomes easier. Better data quality means better visibility. Better visibility means better decisions. I'm sharing a few of the common challenges I've come across in industrial data environments in the infographic below. Would be interested to hear from others working with PI System, industrial historians, OT/IT integration or manufacturing data — what challenges do you see most often? #AVEVAPI #PISystem #IndustrialData #DataHistorian #Manufacturing #OTIT #IndustrialIoT #DataManagement","reactionCount":3,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Jake Hutchings","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jake-hutchings-5bb7a4167/","jobTitle":"Interested in talking to retiring IFAs to help maximise their full potential by finding the most appropriate acquirer for you and your clients","company":"","location":"","postText":"How much is your CRM really costing your advice firm? Not just in licence fees. In duplicated workflows. In disconnected systems. In manual reporting. In wasted adviser and paraplanner time. What if one platform could bring everything together? Integrated CRM, AI-powered meeting transcription, Portfolio aggregation & reporting, Income reconciliation, Market data access, Investment comparison & transfer tools, Role-specific workflows for advisers, paraplanners, finance teams and management. All within one connected ecosystem built specifically for UK financial advice firms. Through our relationship with the provider, the premium version is currently available completely free of charge, with no licence fees and no per-user costs. Less complexity. More efficiency. Better client outcomes. If you're reviewing your current CRM or technology stack, let's have a conversation. #IFA #FinancialPlanning #WealthManagement #AdviceTech #FinancialAdvice #CRM #AI #WealthTech #FinancialServices","reactionCount":2,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Budur Khayat","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/budurkhayat/","jobTitle":"Information Systems | Data & BI Analyst | Business Analyst | CRM Implementation","company":"","location":"","postText":"Bright Academy Project. The Dashboard is not just a data display tool, it is a final output for a comprehensive project that started with building the CRM structure and ended with data analysis and converting it into Dashboards and indicators that support extracting Business Insights and decision-making. The project was applied to Bright Academy using Zoho CRM and Zoho Analytics, with trial data for display purposes. The project went through several main stages: 1. CRM Design & Configuration - Building and customizing the CRM structure to align with work requirements and processes. 2. Master Data Management - Organizing Master Data and standardizing basic data to ensure consistency. 3. Data Preparation & Migration - Preparing data and standardizing values and formats, then importing and linking to appropriate Modules. 4. Data Quality & Validation - Verifying data completeness, accuracy and consistency. 5. Data Analysis & KPI Development - Analyzing operational data and identifying KPIs. 6. Dashboard Development - Converting analysis results into 4 Dashboards: Executive Dashboard, Marketing Dashboard, Academic Dashboard, and Sales Dashboard. The goal is to convert operational data into organized information providing clear visibility around Performance, Sales Pipeline, Revenue, and KPIs, supporting Data-Driven Decision Making.","reactionCount":20,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Techthaastu","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/techthaastu/posts/","jobTitle":"","company":"Techthaastu","location":"","postText":"Your Business Has Plenty of Data. The Problem Is Nobody Owns It. A client changes their phone number. One person updates Excel. Another has the old number in WhatsApp. The CRM has something else. The billing system has another version. Three months later, someone asks: Which one is correct? This is not a database problem. It is a data ownership problem. In growing professional-service businesses, the same client information often appears in: CRM, Excel, Accounting software, Email, WhatsApp, Documents, Individual employee records. The dangerous part is not duplicate data. It is conflicting data. Because once two systems disagree, employees start becoming the integration layer. A mature digital system should establish: One source of truth → defined owner → controlled updates → connected workflows. Before asking: Which software should we buy? Ask: Where should the truth live? That single question can change the architecture of an entire business. #DataManagement #BusinessSoftware #DigitalTransformation #Operations #CAFirm #LegalTech #InsurTech","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"EAVE","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/eave-capital/posts/","jobTitle":"","company":"EAVE","location":"","postText":"Five compliance gaps. One governance layer. POPIA's gap between policy and practice. FICA's record-keeping standard most systems weren't built for. SARS's burden of proof when records can't be produced. The Companies Act and King's board-level accountability for records integrity. FSCA and FAIS's documentation standard for every piece of financial advice given. Regulatory Information Intelligence addresses all five through a single governance layer across your existing ERP, CRM, email and document management environments. No migration. No disruption to how your teams already work. Delivered through OpenText, calibrated to South African law, by the only accredited partner combining both. The question isn't whether you can afford to invest in governance. It's whether you can afford to keep operating without it. Speak to EAVE about an assessment. #RegulatoryInformationIntelligence #OpenText #COMPLYintel #ComplianceSA #POPIA #FICA","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"IFA client data management","postUrl":"","authorName":"Rebecca Parker-Binks","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/rebecca-parker-binks-59b5a21a9/","jobTitle":"Executive Recruitment Consultant ISE Partners Ltd | Recruitment to the Investment Sector | isepartners.com Part of Pertemps Network Group | London","company":"ISE Partners","location":"London","postText":"Client Services Executive (CSE) London | 08:00–16:30 | 1 day WFH after probation £31,000–£33,000 + excellent benefits. Looking to build your career in wealth and investment management? This is a fantastic opportunity for an early-career financial services professional (1–3 years' experience) to join a highly respected, independent investment management firm within their Professional Adviser Services team. This role places you at the centre of the business, working closely with IFAs, intermediaries, and front-office teams to deliver exceptional client service and seamless operations. You'll be: Acting as a key contact for IFAs and intermediaries, Supporting onboarding, KYC, and regulatory processes, Preparing client reporting and valuations, Processing portfolio instructions and payments, Collaborating across Operations, Compliance, and Data teams. Ideal for someone with IFA or wealth management experience who thrives in a busy environment, enjoys building relationships, and takes pride in accuracy. A brilliant next step for someone looking to grow long-term within financial services.","reactionCount":5,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]}]}


