{"posts":[{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Francis Property Solutions LLC","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/francis-property-solutions-llc-37681738b/","jobTitle":"Business Owner","company":"Francis Property Solutions LLC","location":"","postText":"The Landlord Question. If you're a landlord, ask yourself: \"If I didn't look at my property for six months, what would I be worried about finding?\" That answer is probably where your maintenance system needs improvement. Maybe it's landscaping. Maybe it's trash. Maybe it's leaks. Maybe it's exterior damage. Maybe it's tenant turnover. Your biggest concern is often telling you where your biggest operational weakness is.","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Gwendolyn Regan","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/gwendolyn-regan-61b27594/","jobTitle":"Affordable Housing Professional | SME & Enablement Lead | PropTech | HCCP | CPO","company":"","location":"","postText":"203A MAT Guide has been posted! 30 day comment period begins now. Links to HUD.gov Tenant Rental Assistance Certification System (TRACS).","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Kieran Crosbie","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kieran-crosbie-98361532a/","jobTitle":"Founder @ Synon One | Building Smarter Ways to Manage Property","company":"Synon One","location":"","postText":"LANDLORDS: A £100 MAINTENANCE JOB CAN BECOME A £1,000 PROBLEM VERY QUICKLY. The expensive part of maintenance often isn't the original problem. It's the delay. A small leak gets ignored. Moisture spreads. Flooring gets damaged. A ceiling needs repaired. Decoration needs redone. Suddenly the original problem is the cheapest part of the job. There's a simple lesson here: Don't just record maintenance. Track it until it's finished. For every issue, you should know: What happened? When was it reported? How urgent is it? Who is dealing with it? What is the current status? How much has it cost? Is it actually complete? This becomes increasingly important as a portfolio grows. Good maintenance management doesn't just keep tenants happy. It protects the asset. This is exactly why maintenance tracking became an important part of what we're building with Synon One.","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/property-management-kenya-doesnt-have-mean-spreadsheets-nmxff/","authorName":"FANSOFT SOLUTIONS","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/fansoft-solutions/posts/","jobTitle":"","company":"FANSOFT SOLUTIONS","location":"","postText":"It's the 5th of the month. Do you actually know who's paid? For most landlords and property managers in Kenya, rent collection still means scrolling through M-Pesa messages one by one, hoping nothing was missed. Tenapay replaces that guesswork with automated rent collection, real-time payment tracking, and portfolio-wide visibility, built specifically for the African rental market. With Tenapay, you get: Auto-Rent Collection, Portfolio Management, Compliance & Audits, Maintenance Tracking, Real-Time Analytics. No more chasing payments. No more manual reconciliation. Just a clear, live picture of every property, every tenant, every shilling collected. Built by Fansoft Solutions. #Tenapay #PropertyManagement #RentCollection #RealEstateKenya #Proptech #MPesa #LandlordTools #PropertyManagementSoftware #KenyaRealEstate #FansoftSolutions #RealEstateTech #RentalManagement","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Landio","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/getlandio/posts/","jobTitle":"","company":"Landio","location":"","postText":"We've built Landio — property management software for UK landlords who are done paying letting agents. The average letting agent charges 10-15% of monthly rent. On a £1,500 property that's £2,700 a year — for admin work that software can handle. Landio handles tenant onboarding, compliance tracking, rent collection, maintenance requests and document management — all in one platform built specifically for UK self-managing landlords. Try it free for 14 days — no card required. 🔗 getlandio.com","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Spring Morgan","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/spring-morgan-885645187/","jobTitle":"Office Cleaning, AirBnB, residential","company":"","location":"","postText":"Smart Tips for Property Maintenance Coordination - a planning-first approach that reduces gaps between routine upkeep, guest turnover, and tenant readiness. I share the practical checklist I use: a maintenance calendar, preventive inspections, bundled service days, clear tenant communication, and a central coordinator to manage cleaners, handymen, and vendors so properties stay guest-ready with fewer surprises. 🏡 If you manage vacation rentals, offices, or homes in Santa Cruz or San Jose, this field-tested guide walks through the steps you can implement today to save time and avoid last-minute fixes. Read the full post to get actionable next steps - and tell me which upkeep task costs you the most time so we can troubleshoot it together. #PropertyManagement #VacationRentals #MaintenanceStrategy","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Steven Lunetta","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/steven-lunetta-92055519/","jobTitle":"Property Manager | Real Estate Broker, Certified Property Manager","company":"Home Showings Property Management","location":"Sacramento and Elk Grove","postText":"📊 We published a practical guide for Sacramento and Elk Grove rental owners: Property Management Financial Reporting Software - A Landlord's Guide to Transparency. Transparent reporting replaces scattered receipts with real oversight: real‑time dashboards, owner portals, automated expense categorization, and Schedule E-ready statements. 🛡️ The guide explains how these systems keep your books audit‑ready, simplify tax prep, and give you a single source of truth for rent collection and maintenance spending. We pair professional reporting tools with local Elk Grove expertise so your data is accurate and contextually relevant. #PropertyManagement #FinancialReporting #ElkGrove","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Virtual Assistant Talent, LLC","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/virtual-assistant-talent-llc/posts/","jobTitle":"","company":"Virtual Assistant Talent, LLC","location":"","postText":"🚨 40 hours a month. That's what rental property admin work can cost a landlord who's doing it all solo. 🏠 Tenant communication and screening 📄 Lease renewals and documentation 💵 Rent collection tracking 🔧 Coordinating maintenance requests 📊 Keeping records organized across properties A Rental Property Admin VA takes these repetitive landlord tasks off your plate — so you can focus on growing your portfolio instead of chasing paperwork. We broke down exactly where landlords lose the most time and how a dedicated VA can give it back. 👉 Read the full article: Rental Property Admin VA — Streamline Landlord Workflows. If you got 40 hours back this month, what would you do with them? #RentalProperty #Landlord #PropertyManagement #RealEstateVA #VirtualAssistant #PropertyManager #BusinessGrowth #Delegation","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Chandler Janger","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chandlerjanger/","jobTitle":"Business Development Manager","company":"Spectrum Realty Services","location":"Jacksonville, FL","postText":"🔑 A Great Tenant Isn't Just About Paying Rent on Time. When choosing a tenant, there's more to consider than whether they can afford the monthly rent. A strong screening process can help landlords evaluate things like: • Rental history • Income and employment • Credit history • Background check • Previous evictions • Overall application consistency. The goal isn't to find the perfect tenant—it's to make an informed decision and reduce unnecessary risk. The right screening process can make a big difference in the long-term success of a rental property. #PropertyManagement #JacksonvilleFL #Landlords #RentalProperty #RealEstateInvesting #JacksonvillePropertyManagement","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Maimoona Shekkeer","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"","company":"GetSmartLease","location":"","postText":"Are we measuring the real cost of rent payment friction? Transaction fees are easy to measure. The hours spent reconciling payments, answering tenant questions, correcting records, and following up on overdue balances are easier to overlook. Our latest article explores how these small inefficiencies add up—and why reducing payment friction becomes increasingly important as rental portfolios grow. 🔗 Read here: https://lnkd.in/gar77xi2. How much of your payment process is still manual? #PropertyManagement #SmartPayments #RentCollection #PropTech","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Md. Miron Sheikh","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"","company":"Pandarly","location":"","postText":"\"For anyone running a rental operation: how are you currently handling maintenance scheduling on equipment that's constantly rotating between customers? Manual tracking, a tool, or mostly reactive?\"","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant maintenance tracking","postUrl":"","authorName":"Steve Stasiuk","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/maninnewport/","jobTitle":"Business Development Manager | Performance-Based Property Management | Affordable Housing & Residential Investment Properties","company":"Stonelink Property Management","location":"","postText":"When it comes to affordable housing, maintenance is more than fixing what's broken—it's part of compliance, resident retention, and long-term asset stewardship. Data from Property Meld (which happens to be the maintenance platform we currently use) reinforces something strong operators already understand: better maintenance processes are connected to faster repairs, better communication, lower costs and improved resident satisfaction. For housing authorities and affordable housing providers, the stakes can be even higher. A successful maintenance operation requires: • Dedicated processes and accountability for work orders and inspections • In-house maintenance resources capable of responding quickly and consistently • Technology and data to track response times, recurring issues, costs and completion • Documentation that helps support HUD, LIHTC and other affordable housing compliance requirements. Deferred or poorly documented maintenance doesn't just inconvenience residents. It can create inspection deficiencies, increase operating costs and ultimately put the performance of the property at risk. #AffordableHousing #PropertyManagement #HousingAuthorities #LIHTC #HUD #MaintenanceManagement #AssetManagement","reactionCount":7,"commentCount":1,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]}]}


