Url":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/gwendolyn-regan-61b27594/","jobTitle":"Affordable Housing Professional | SME & Enablement Lead | PropTech | HCCP | CPO","company":"","location":"","postText":"203A MAT Guide has been posted! 30 day comment period begins now… Tenant Rental Assistance Certification System (TRACS)","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant query response delays","postUrl":"","authorName":"Central Rentals Canada","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/central-rentals-edmonton/posts/","jobTitle":"Company Page","company":"Central Rentals Canada","location":"","postText":"Missing a notice period by just one day in Alberta results in the RTDRS (Residential Tenancy Dispute Resolution Service) completely resetting the eviction process, which can cause significant delays. The standard notice periods vary across provinces: in Alberta, it's three months for own-use; in Ontario, an N12 notice requires 60 days; British Columbia mandates four months; and Quebec specifies six months for mid-term evictions. Always serve notices early, retain proof of service, and file a copy with the tribunal on the same day to ensure proper documentation. By 2026, every Canadian landlord should ideally have automated systems for: • Provincial lease generation covering all 13 provinces and territories, • Rent collection with automatic CAD receipts, • Categorized T776 forms tagged month-by-month for tax purposes. Utilize the provincial notice generator tool inside Central Rentals —pre-filled according to lease agreements and automatically filed to your records—to streamline the process.… more","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant query response delays","postUrl":"","authorName":"Central Rentals Canada","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/central-rentals-edmonton/posts/","jobTitle":"Company Page","company":"Central Rentals Canada","location":"","postText":"Rent overdue by 3 days? Send a warning notification to the tenant. If the delay extends to 10 days, file an N4 notice in Ontario or a 14-day notice in Alberta, as required by provincial law. Implement an automated sequence: a friendly reminder on day 3, a formal notice on day 7, a statutory notice on day 10, and file at the tribunal on day 14. All relevant documents are automatically saved to the tenant's file for legal record-keeping. By 2026, every Canadian landlord should have automation in place for these three essential tools: • A provincial lease generator compatible with all 13 provinces and territories. • Rent collection system with automated receipts, supporting payments in Canadian dollars (CAD). • Categorized tracking of income and expenses with T776 forms, organized month-by-month for easy reporting. Enable auto-dunning to automatically send reminders to tenants who are late on payments inside Central Rentals. This feature is reversible within 24 hours if the tenant makes a payment. #PropertyManagement #Canada #CanadianRealEstate #Landlords #SaaS… more","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant query response delays","postUrl":"","authorName":"Rob Tregenza","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/robtregenza/","jobTitle":"CMO & Co-Founder, levelheaded | Human-centered resolution, accelerated by AI","company":"","location":"","postText":"Most residents do not want to leave. They want to be heard. Property management has spent years optimizing for efficiency. Almost none of that optimization has touched the moment conflict starts. That gap is where trust breaks down and where good residents decide to leave. Behavioral intelligence and early intervention are finally entering the PropTech conversation in a real way in 2026. 12-day average resolution. 75% rent recovery rate. Faster resolution is not just an operational win. It is a human one. What does your current process say to a resident in the middle of a dispute? #PropertyManagement #PropTech #ResidentRetention #HumanCenteredDesign #Levelheaded… more","reactionCount":1,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"tenant query response delays","postUrl":"","authorName":"RefCheckers","authorUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/refcheckers/posts/","jobTitle":"Company Page","company":"RefCheckers","location":"","postText":"Say goodbye to tenant screening headaches 🏠 For property managers and landlords, finding the right tenant is a race against the clock. Vacant properties cost money, but rushing into a lease without proper reference checks is a huge risk. Standard reference checks often mean playing phone tag with former landlords or deciphering vague email replies. With RefCheckers, tenant screening becomes effortless: 1️⃣ Send an automated request in seconds. 2","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]}]}


