service schedule during shoulder seasons.\nHere is how your database dictates your ad spend strategy:\n- Small Database (<300 members / $1M revenue): High ad spend required. Prioritize paid search to drive instant demand and convert calls into maintenance members.","reactionCount":10,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"3","postUrl":"","authorName":"Dharshini Sethuraman","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Computer Science Engineering Student | Problem Solving | Learning Web Development & DSA","company":"","location":"","postText":"🎫 Built a Hostel Maintenance Ticketing System!\nI built a work order system that lets students raise repair/maintenance requests for their hostel rooms, instead of relying on word-of-mouth complaints that get lost.\n3️⃣ Status and comments update as the issue gets addressed\n📚 What I learned:\nBuilding this helped me think through real-world UX for a request-tracking system — form validation, state management for ticket status, and designing a dashboard that's actually easy to scan.\n🔗 GitHub: https://lnkd.in/gZ6EnvFX\n#WebDevelopment #StudentProject #FullStack #LearningByBuilding #ProjectManagement","reactionCount":11,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"4","postUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/why-do-we-spend-millions-maintenance-still-have-unexpected-uzgef/","authorName":"Yosra Hoveizavy","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"CEO at SeaMaster Co | SeaTrade Maritime 20 Under 40 Finalist 2025 ; Ex IMO GOODWILL MARITIME AMBASSADOR - 4 YEARS | Bridging the gap between sea and software — making maritime management less stormy, more smart.","company":"SeaMaster Co","location":"","postText":"🤔 Do you think a high maintenance budget automatically means a more reliable vessel?\nI don't❗\nAcross many fleets, recurring defects, repeated spare consumption, rising repair costs and machinery downtime can continue even when maintenance plans are being followed.\nThat is why I believe shipowners should look beyond how much is being spent and ask a more important question: is that spending actually improving vessel reliability?\nI shared this article because better maintenance decisions start with better visibility into the patterns behind the work orders.\nI'd be interested to hear from shipowners, technical managers and superintendents:\n⁉️ What indicator do you trust most when judging whether your maintenance strategy is really working?\n#shipping #shipowner #maritime #planned_maintenance_system","reactionCount":13,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"5","postUrl":"","authorName":"Steven Khenaisser","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Owner, Cedar Maintenance & More | Property Maintenance for SF Property Managers | Unit Turns • Painting • Flooring • Plumbing • Electrical • Renovations","company":"Cedar Maintenance & More","location":"","postText":"Not every maintenance request has the same level of urgency.\nEffective work-order triage helps property teams respond appropriately:\n🔴 Emergency: Active flooding, fire hazards, gas odors, loss of essential services, or immediate safety risks\n🟠 Urgent: Active leaks, failed entry locks, significant drain backups, or conditions that may quickly cause additional damage\n🟡 Routine: Minor repairs, adjustments, cosmetic damage, and noncritical fixture issues\nCorrectly categorizing requests helps protect tenants, reduce property damage, and keep technicians focused on the highest-priority work.\nGood maintenance begins before the technician arrives—it begins with the right information.","reactionCount":0,"commentCount":0,"discoveredAt":"2026-09-03","interactions":[]},{"topicId":"6","postUrl":"","authorName":"Mark W. Melby","authorUrl":"","jobTitle":"Founder & CEO @ Aloft Evermōr | Aircraft Maintenance Management Software","company":"Aloft Evermōr","location":"","postText":"Great info from Jet Support Services, Inc. (JSSI)\nIn Phase & On Time: Why Tolerances Matter in Maintenance T